Negative control for the armed-and-waiting statement (`R7-5`).

Empties the hint catalogue and leaves everything else — the chip still names the
preset, the frame still glows, the worker still serves the recorded refusal on
the next write — so the only claim that can go red is the ruled one: a preset
that cannot show itself the moment it is armed says so. `error-action` answers a
WRITE, so with the statement gone the page is armed and visibly unchanged, which
is the control-that-does-nothing the ruling refused to ship.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the forced-canvas pending case — an armed `error-action` renders a
statement beside its chip, and the other presets render none.

